It is Wednesday, six o'clock.
I am in the café.
I meet my neighbour.
Frau Krüger is already there.
We order coffee.
We drink the coffee and talk.
"How do you find Berlin, Frau Flores?" asks Frau Krüger.
"The city is great," I answer.
Frau Krüger smiles warmly.
"We are neighbours," she says.
"Shall we simply say 'du'?" she then asks.
"I am Sabine."
I smile too.
"Very gladly," I say.
"My name is Maya."
"Do you always drink coffee at this time, Maya?" asks Sabine.
"No, only sometimes," I answer.
We sit in the café for another hour.
I am very happy about my new friend.
